## Style Logic Separation

### Separate Style Functions from Components

**✅ Best Practice:**

```typescript
// Separated, testable, reusable
const getTextStyle = (theme: Theme, variant: Variant, size: Size) => {
  const token = theme.text[variant][size]
  return css({
    fontSize: `${token.fontSize}px`,
    fontWeight: token.fontWeight,
    lineHeight: `${token.lineHeight}px`,
    letterSpacing: `${token.letterSpacing}px`,
  })
}

const Component = () => {
  return (
    <Element css={(theme: Theme) => getTextStyle(theme, variant, size)} />
  )
}
```

**Benefits:**

- Testable: Can test style logic independently
- Reusable: Can share across components
- Maintainable: Clear separation of concerns
- Type-safe: Full theme type inference

**❌ Avoid inline styles:**

```typescript
// ❌ Hard to test, not reusable
<Element css={css`
  font-size: ${theme.text[variant][size].fontSize}px;
`} />
```

